Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:14:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ga2_fileread: the platform code in a source file (no
 <windows.h> in the header)

The header pulled in <windows.h>, whose macros (EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT and others) clash with the runtime's enum
names: the Windows release build failed in ps2_disc_mount.cpp once ga2_fileread.h was included before
ps2_runtime.h (and Support.h now includes it in every stub). The handle is kept as a pointer-sized integer and the
CreateFileW/ReadFile and open/pread code moved to src/lib/ga2_fileread.cpp (the launcher compiles it too).

Verified: Linux build and unit tests 661/662; x86_64-w64-mingw32 syntax check of ps2_disc_mount.cpp,
bvr_assets.cpp, Kernel/Stubs/CD.cpp and ga2_movie.cpp with the build's flags.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
